From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Subject: [PATCH] EDEN_UP_UPLOAD_RUNS=1: batch in-order stream uploads and fuse dispatch barriers

Port of zortos293/Lichii #1245 (4d7412ac), #1246 (7fcfb641), handle jpkto.
One switch tests the pair; off by default. Includes #805 transfer ordering already
optional in 0471, automatically enabled for this arm. No temporal replacement path
exists in our DispatchCompute. Preserve COMPUTE_INDIRECT_ORDER when fusing indirect.
Every RecordWithUploadBuffer, handoff and submission first closes the pending run.
Logs "EDEN_UP_UPLOAD_RUNS: <n> runs, <m> copies" at the 1st, 2nd, 4th ... run.
v2 (review): the indirect dispatch lambda no longer captures the static indirect_order
(clang: cannot capture a variable without automatic storage duration).
Test the door with split/ahead guard both on and off, readbacks and rewritten uploads;
compare barrier/command counts, captures and frame times. Validate Vulkan hazards.

